Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: SM-T825 thermal protection and verified current limits

Use the stock PM8994 ADC channels and charge-enable GPIO. Fail closed on
sensor/control errors; cap BC1.2 ports at 1.5 A and verify writes on every
policy pass. Battery status follows the charger, including low net current.
The board calibration/policy header is installed by prepare-lte-kernel.py.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/Kconfig
@@ -302,7 +302,7 @@
 
 config BATTERY_SM5705
 	tristate "Silicon Mitus SM5705 fuel gauge"
-	depends on I2C
+	depends on I2C && IIO
 	help
 	  Read-only driver for the fuel gauge part of the Silicon Mitus SM5705,
 	  as used in the Samsung Galaxy Tab S3. It reports battery voltage,
@@ -310,10 +310,10 @@
 
 config CHARGER_SM5705
 	tristate "Silicon Mitus SM5705 charger"
-	depends on I2C
-	help
-	  Read-only driver for the charger part of the Silicon Mitus SM5705:
-	  cable presence, charging state, health and current limits.
+	depends on I2C && IIO && GPIOLIB
+	help
+	  SM-T825 charging control, temperature monitoring and fail-closed
+	  current limits for the Silicon Mitus SM5705.
 
